  data: {
    LLM: 'Aim for five unpaired low cards. Remember opponents can use one of your board cards; avoid exposing cards that complete strong lows for others. Position matters for betting.\n\nTrack which board cards help which opponents. Bet to force folds and remove a key board card from the table. Ace-to-five low: wheel (5-4-3-2-A) is the nuts.\n\nStrategic folding to deny an opponent the board card they need. Represent strength by betting when your board looks weak. Pot limit amplifies implied odds.',
    Player: 'Aim for five unpaired low cards. Remember opponents can use one of your board cards; avoid exposing cards that complete strong lows for others. Position matters for betting.\n\nTrack which board cards help which opponents. Bet to force folds and remove a key board card from the table. Ace-to-five low: wheel (5-4-3-2-A) is the nuts.\n\nStrategic folding to deny an opponent the board card they need. Represent strength by betting when your board looks weak. Pot limit amplifies implied odds.',
